  clock: 11  # feff
  nonce: feff  # feff
  message: "GATE 4 PARTIALLY CLEARED. INV-sukoh is satisfied (PR #587, dev 1a3145c9f0), so\nthe row-denominator half of this gate is closed. Remaining before the first\ndatum: the INV-nular and INV-fumod remainders, both still violated.\n\nWHAT IT CHANGES FOR THE PRE-REGISTRATION, and it is not what the item implied.\nINV-sukoh was filed as row-unit-only on the grounds that INV-karud's situation\ncollapse absorbs the doubling. That holds only for {structural, ddg_mixed}: a\nconfirmed ddg walk is a pair claim and passes through collapse untouched, so on\nthe ddg arm the doubling produced two SITUATIONS. 0005's population happened to\nbe structural and ddg_mixed, which is why it measured as row-only there. A\npre-registered cohort with a different method mix would have inherited a\nsituation-level inflation nobody had sized.\n\nSIZE, measured A/B on the two repositories INV-sukoh names (per-arm cache, arms\nstrictly sequential, arm proven before each run):\n  mitmproxy  summed collapsed_flow_count 29 -> 20 (-31.0%)\n  poetry     summed collapsed_flow_count  5 ->  3 (-40.0%)\n  situation counts unchanged on both; 8 of 8 claim verdicts unchanged.\nThis is a bigger row-side move than 0005's 5.3% because 0005 measured over a\n5-repo census while this is the two repositories where the shape concentrates.\nTagged awaits_bakeoff_validation; whether it generalises is unvalidated.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE ESTIMATOR DECLARATION: any row-unit figure taken before\n1a3145c9f0 is not comparable to one taken after, on Python substrate. That is\nnow the SECOND such discontinuity this leg has produced -- PR #541's bash\n\"> /dev/null\" fix is the other, and it accounts for 6 of the 11 deductions in\n0006's re-derived useful precision. The pre-registration should state the\nmerged-tree SHA the series starts from, not just the date."  # feff
- op: discuss  # 576d
  at: '2026-08-28T07:07:02Z'  # 576d
  by: agent  # 576d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 576d
  clock: 12  # 576d
  nonce: 576d  # 576d
  message: "DEPENDENCY DISCHARGED BY DECLARATION, NOT BY REPAIR (removing INV-linub's\nisbefore edge to this item; rationale recorded there too).\n\nI had made INV-linub block this item because five to six languages structurally\nproduce ZERO taint flows, so a fifteen-language benchmark cohort would be a\nthree-language cohort wearing a fifteen-language label -- this item's own\n\"two-repo cohort wearing a five-repo label\", one level up.\n\nThat reading was right about the hazard and wrong about the remedy. Fixing it\nis RECALL work, and WI-sivuz's standing band stops recall while precision is\nbelow it (\"<50%: precision is the headline problem and recall work should stop\nuntil it is understood\"; the later useful band is \"<=25% useful\"). 0006 useful\nprecision is 24.1%, below both.\n\nSO THE PRE-REGISTRATION MUST CARRY A LANGUAGE SCOPE, and that is a requirement\non THIS item rather than a blocker from another. Concretely, when the benchmark\nis pre-registered it must declare:\n  - the languages in scope, and the languages EXCLUDED BY NAME;\n  - for each exclusion, the reason and its item (INV-linub for the >=87%\n    method-kind group: java, scala, kotlin, objc, swift);\n  - that an excluded language is EXCLUDED, not measured-at-zero -- a zero from\n    a language whose sinks are structurally unreachable is not a datapoint\n    about the tool's precision, and pooling it in is the same undeclared\n    estimator choice this item was raised about;\n  - the SHA. 18 commits changed taint between the 08-25 screen and the 08-27\n    figures, so attribution across that boundary is not recoverable.\n\nDoing it this way also makes the exclusion REVERSIBLE and VISIBLE: when the\nband lifts and INV-linub closes, the excluded languages enter the cohort as a\ndeclared scope change with a named before/after, which is exactly the\ncomparability this item exists to buy."  # 576d
